1
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Belê temaşevanin hêja..
 
Yes, dear viewers...

2
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Vê hefteyê em ê berê xwe bidin çiyayê Lêlûn, navçeya Şêrawa.
 
This week we will head to the Lilon Mountain, in the Sherawa
district.

3
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Gundekî herî mezin di navçeya Şêrawa da, navê gund jî Gundê
Mezin e.
 
The largest village in the Sherawa district, the name of the
village is Gundê Mezin (The Big Village).

4
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Ev gund li ser sînor dikeve. Navbera Efrînê û Helebê da
dikeve.
 
This village is located on the border. It's situated between
Afrin and Aleppo.

5
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Cîranên vî gundî hemî gundên Ereban e.
 
The neighbors of this village are all Arab villages.

6
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Ev gund beriya vê bi şêst salî, hemî Êzîdî bûn. Zeredeştî
bûn.
 
Sixty years ago, this village was entirely Ezidi. They were
Zoroastrian.

7
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Piştî wê, hinek bûn misilman, hinek jî mane li ser ola xwe
mane, Êzîdî mane.
 
After that, some became Muslims, and some remained in their
religion, they remained Ezidi.

8
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Dike vê hefteyê em derbasî vî gundî bibin.
 
Let's enter this village this week.

9
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Gundê Mezin, gundekî navçeya Şêrawa ya Efrînê ye.
 
Gundê Mezin, a village in the Sherawa district of Afrin.

10
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
40 kîlometreyî başûr, rojhilatê bajarê Efrînê dikeve.
 
It is located 40 kilometers southeast of the city of Afrin.

11
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Gund 500 sal berê, li ser quntara Çiyayê Lêlûnê..
 
500 years ago, on the foothills of the Lilon Mountain...

12
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
ji aliyê Kurdên Êzîdî va hatiye avakirin.
 
it was built by Ezidi Kurds.

13
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Naha jî bi qasî 260 malên ku ji Kurdên Êzîdî û Misilman pêk
tên di gund de jiyan dikin.
 
Even now, there are about 260 households consisting of Ezidi
and Muslim Kurds living in the village.

14
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Şêniyên gund piştî demeke gundên Bircelqos û Kîlotê, nezikî
gundê xwe ava kirin.
 
Later, the villagers built the villages of Burj Al Qas and
Kilote, near their village.

15
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Ji ber siyasetên înkar û zordariyê...
 
Due to the policies of denial and oppression...

16
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
ku ji aliyê rejîma Baasê va li ser gundiyan dihatin
meşandin...
 
carried out against the villagers by the Baath regime...

17
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:40,000
gelek şêniyên gund bûn misilman.
 
many villagers became Muslim.

18
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Baas gundê Mezin ji daîreya wê ya Efrînê qut kiribû...
 
The Baath had cut off Gundê Mezin from its Afrin
department...

19
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
û bi bajarokê Niblê ve girêdabû.
 
and connected it to the town of Nubl.

20
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Di pêngava Şoreşa Rojava da..
 
In the Rojava Revolution campaign...

21
00:02:49,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Gundê Mezin careke din vegeriya hembeza daîreya xwe ya
Efrînê.
 
Gundê Mezin returned to the embrace of its Afrin department
once again.

22
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Merheba Apê Hesen.
 
Hello Apê Hesen.

23
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
Merheba ehlen wesehlen.
 
Hello, welcome.

24
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Apê Hesen ev gundê we çend sal di ava bûye?
 
Apê Hesen, how old is your village?

25
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Welleh ev ... teqrîben pênc sed sal di nav e. Çar sed pênc
sed heye.
 
By God, this... it's approximately five hundred years old.
It's four, five hundred years.

26
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Ev gundê mezin ev navê mezin ji ku hatiye?
 
This Gundê Mezin, where did this name "Mezin" (Big) come
from?

27
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Va navê.. ev gund e, xerabeyên xwe, perên wî, mesahata xwe
fireh e.
 
This name... this village, its ruins, its borders, its area
is wide.

28
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Wê maneyê gundê mezin e.
 
For that reason, it's the big village.

29
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Yanî gundekî... zeviyên xwe pirr in, fireh e?
 
Meaning it's a village with many wide fields?

30
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Xerabeyên xwe pir in, gundê xwe, em bêjin çend xarabe xwe
hene. Şeş, heft, heşt, xarabe xwe hene.
 
Its ruins are many. It's village, let's say it has several
ruins. It has six, seven, eight ruins.

31
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Berê li çine? Ev xarabe çi nene? Berê mal li wira de bûn?
 
Before what are these ruins? Did they live there before?

32
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Asarên qedîme. Asar e.
 
Ancient relics. It's ruins.

33
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Û gundê herî mezin di Şêrawa da gundê we ye.
 
And the biggest village in Sherawa is your village.

34
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Gundê mezin e.. gundê me.
 
It's the big village.. our village.

35
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Jiber ku ev navê mezin ji wira hatiye.
 
Because this name "Mezin" comes from here.

36
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Di Şêrawa da gundê herî mezin gundê we ye.
 
Your village is the biggest one in Sherawa.

37
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Apê Hesen çend malbat di gundê we da hene?
 
Apê Hesen, how many families are in your village?

38
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Heft malbat hene li vira...
 
There are seven families here...

39
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Kanim navê wan bêjî ji bo me?
 
Can you tell us their names?

40
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Temam... kerem bike...
 
Alright... here you go...

41
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Malbata.. Mala Bûdeq.
 
The family of.. The Bûdeq Family.

42
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Mala Hemo.
 
The Hemo Family.

43
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Mala Kuko.
 
The Kuko Family.

44
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Mala Cimo.
 
The Cimo Family.

45
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Mala Ûskê.
 
The Uske Family.

46
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Mala Hasî.
 
The Hasi Family.

47
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Mala Elêwî.
 
The Elewi Family.

48
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Bûn heft...
 
That makes seven...

49
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Bûn heft malbat.
 
That makes seven families.

50
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Em dest xweş dikin, spas dikin apê Hesen.
 
We bless your hands, thank you Apê Hesen.

51
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Ehlen wesehlen heval.
 
Welcome friend.

52
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Belê naha em ê vegerin cem vî milêmê çepê jî, Apê Ûs..
 
Yes, now we will turn to this old man on the left, Apê Us...

53
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
dibêje tiştin ketine bîra wî.
 
he says he remembered some things.

54
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Apê Ûs te ji kû çi tê bîra te?
 
Apê Us, what do you remember?

55
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Ege tê bîra me...
 
Well what comes to my mind...

56
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Berê.. gotin Fransa, û Ereb, û tade yanî di hevdidit in...
 
Before... they said France, and Arabs, and they were
experiencing oppression...

57
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Ev dema tu zarok..
 
That was when you were a child...

58
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Yanî ez dehe, davzde salî.. ha neha..
 
Meaning I was ten, twelve years old... around that...

59
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Paşê me bihîst, me nedî, me bihîst.. gotin Îngilîz hat,
Fransa ji Sûriyê derxist.
 
Later we heard, we didn't see it, we heard.. they said the
English came, and removed France from Syria.

60
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:39,000
Naha tê bîra te, dema ew fransalî li vir bûn tê bîra te?
 
Now you remember, do you remember when the French were here?

61
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Tê bîra min. Me mast bi heşa keran, ba erebatên berê, em
çûne Helebê.
 
I remember. We used to take yogurt on donkeys, with the old
carts, we went to Aleppo.

62
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Yanî.. pê heşa kerê.. em çûne Helebê.
 
Meaning... with the donkey... we went to Aleppo.

63
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Paşê.. û qule.. deriyê Helebê.. û fransawî tê da bûn..
 
Later... that tower... the gate of Aleppo... and the French
were in it...

64
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Şeş tanq derketin.. ketin xwar, li hastî bazen dgeriyan..
 
Six tanks came out... they went down, moving on the
cobblestones...

65
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Hat didgerran.
 
They came around.

66
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Digo qole rabe.. te çi hey, qomê kevne drîye a sar me dake û
her e.
 
He was saying get up... what's wrong with you, throw your
old thorns on us and go.

67
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Û em çûne Enedanê me da danê, û em paşê bhat hasîn em çûn.
 
And we went to Anadan and placed it, and then rested a bit
and we went.

68
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Naha te got Fransa berê li vir bû...
 
Now you said the French were here before...

69
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Lı vir, lı Sûrîyê de bûn...
 
Here, they were in Syria...

70
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Ne li Sûriyê... li gund da, li gunda tina bûn?
 
No in Syria... in the village, weren't they in the villages?

71
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Li gunda tina bûn, na...
 
They weren't in the villages, no...

72
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
Bas deriyê gunda bûn.
 
But they were at the entrance of the villages.

73
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Kîjan derî bûn?
 
Which entrances were they?

74
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Wekî em bêjin.. ba Enedanê, Hreytanê, Helebê. Li wira habûn.
 
Like let's say... near Anadan, Hreytan, Aleppo. They were
there.

75
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Ba gundê me de... yanî neketin.
 
In our village... I mean they didn't enter.

76
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Apê Ûs.
 
Apê Us.

77
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Min.. ev gundê we, beriya vê bi 60-70 salî hûn hemî Êzîdî
bûn.
 
I... this village of yours, 60-70 years ago you were all
Ezidi.

78
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Ewa.
 
Yeah.

79
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Hûn çewa bûn misilman? Êrîşek hati ser we? Zilum hat ser we?
 
How did you become Muslim? Was there an attack on you? Did
oppression fall upon you?

80
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Êrîş rakirina ser me..
 
They launched attacks on us.

81
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Kê?
 
Who?

82
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Yanî.. der dora me... Hemî.. e pêşiyê taxtan e.. taxtan êrîş
kirine ser me.. em hindik bûn wan pir bûn...
 
I mean.. our surroundings... Everyone... first the
authorities.. the authorities attacked us.. we were few,
they were many...

83
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Ew çend gundên Ereban li dora we hene derdorê we da?
 
How many Arab villages are around you?

84
00:06:53,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Pir in.. Ereb.. Qibtan, Kêrbeşîn, Enedan, Îqda, Hreytan,
Heyan, Banûn, Nibl, Nixêbl, heta Ezazê.
 
There are many.. Arabs... Qibtan, Kerbeshin, Anadan, Iqda,
Hreytan, Heyan, Banun, Nubl, Nixebl, up to Azaz.

85
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Em a hemî derdora we bûn berê.. êrîş lı we dikirin yanî?
 
They were all around you before.. did they attack you?

86
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Yanî... em qels bûn. Ewa quwetlî bûn me pê nikanî yanî êrîş
ser me dikir yanî.
 
I mean... we were weak. They were powerful, we couldn't
handle them, I mean they attacked us.

87
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Wîn çûn nav wan.. hûn di dan û di stend ba wan?
 
You went among them... did you interact with them?

88
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:23,000
Zê... em têk çûyî bûn ba wan. Cîranê hev bûn... erdê me yek
e, evî pêve peve..
 
Zê... we were integrated with them. We were neighbors... our
land is one, it's connected...

89
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:27,000
Ji ber ku wê gavê mastek we hebû... Ji ber wê mastê we di
birin firotin...
 
Because at that time you had some yogurt... Because of that
you took your yogurt to sell...

90
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Na min got.. me mastê xwe dibira Heleb...
 
No I said.. we used to take our yogurt to Aleppo...

91
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Hûn çawa di çûn Helebê?
 
How did you go to Aleppo?

92
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Em dî kendiya me.. va mastê xwe dida ba hev.. me li kerê bar
dikir em.. Enedanê, bat hesîn... û paşê meşê em çûne
Helebê.. me mastê xwe di firot..
 
We put our sacks... gathered our yogurt.. we would load it
on the donkey... Anadan, rest a bit... and then we walked to
Aleppo.. we would sell our yogurt.

93
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Hûn pêya diçûn, bi meş diçûn?
 
You went on foot, walking?

94
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,000
E meş e meş e..
 
Yes walking, walking...

95
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Çend seeta hûn digihiştin Helebê?
 
How many hours did it take to reach Aleppo?

96
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Yanî.. bûn kin pênc seeat.. ta şeş saet ta.. pênc saet em
digihêştinê.
 
I mean... about five hours.. up to six hours.. we would
arrive in five hours.

97
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Navberê vir û Heleb, çend kîlometr in hene?
 
Between here and Aleppo, how many kilometers are there?

98
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Sî kîlometr e..
 
It's thirty kilometers..

99
00:07:55,000 --> 00:08:00,000
E ne zehmet bû. Berê hûn bi şev diçûn Heleb û hûn bi meş
diçûn..
 
It wasn't difficult. You used to go to Aleppo at night and
walked..

100
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Na em xewkir in... Em dihat ser hişê xwe û şîn dirêj de, me
çav girt û na... heta ser kerê em radizan û em di meşiyan.
Dûr e temaşe, wisa dirêj e.
 
No we slept... We would come to our senses in a long
stretch, closed our eyes and no... we would even sleep on
the donkey and walk. It's far to see, that long.

101
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Cîwa we mastê xwe dikir çi va, û hûn çûn dest xwe dikir..
 
What did you put your yogurt in, and you went and handed it
over...

102
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Elbe, elbe, elbê... em kirine wan elbeyan, şeş kîlo, pênc
kîlo bû her yek... elbê darî... Em.. Me di pêça.. me kerê
dikir.. û ma hekîbek kir e.. kov, ciyê wî, xist turbe..
 
Pails, pails, pails... we put them in those pails, six
kilos, five kilos each... wooden pail... We.. We wrapped
it... put it on the donkey... and had a hekîb (saddlebag)..
kov (sack), its place, put it in the bag..

103
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Ve me da ye, we di xwar. E.. hane va.
 
We gave it, they ate it. Yeah... like that.

104
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:38,000
Yanî, berî hîva re.. we dimeşiyan û diçûn heta sibe.. hûn di
gihîştne Helebê..
 
I mean, before dawn.. you walked and went until morning..
you arrived in Aleppo..

105
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Na, em çûn li Enedanê, piçekî hesîn.
 
No, we went to Anadan, rested a bit.

106
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Nîvî rêk e.. di cihên ba hev de... em li vir dinesîn... û
aha dawara me.. kerê di xwar.. û me careke din bar dikirin,
em çûn.. ta vê rojê e em gehîştin e Helebê.
 
It's halfway.. in places together... we rested here... and
aha our cattle... the donkey ate.. and we loaded again, we
went.. until sunrise we arrived in Aleppo.

107
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Hûn wê afirînê nediçûn?
 
Didn't you go to Afrin?

108
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Efrîn dûr e ji me... ew we nêzîk e ji me.
 
Afrin is far from us... that is closer to us.

109
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Efrîn pirr dûr e..
 
Afrin is very far..

110
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Apê Ûs.. Gundê we.. berê.. girêdayê Niblê bû?
 
Apê Us.. Your village... before... was it connected to Nubl?

111
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Gundê me berê li ser Efrînê bû.
 
Our village was previously attached to Afrin.

112
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Wextê ku neng e.. Hafiz Asad û.. hukm dest xist e û.. yanî
li ser alemê hukm kirî..
 
When that thing.. Hafez Assad and.. took over the rule and..
I mean ruled over the world..

113
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:29,000
Em rakin li ser Niblê.. û li ser Ezazê. Da vê nufûsê me e
ser Niblê ye.
 
They transferred us to Nubl.. and to Azaz. So our registry
is in Nubl.

114
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Ew li wira çen gund girêdayî Niblê bûn?
 
How many villages were attached to Nubl there?

115
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Vê derê... vê derê, Başemre.. Gundê Mezin e, Bircê Kê..
Meyase.. û ewên ku hatin ta sînor de.. hatine.. ta ba me ye.
 
Here... here, Bashemra... Gundê Mezin, Burj Ke.. Meyase..
and those that came up to the border.. came.. up to us.

116
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Bê xeber gundên me yên kurdan di kim. E.. girê daye
Êfrinê... Yanî beriya pêncî, şêst salî hemî girêdayî Efrînê
bûn ..
 
I'm just talking about our Kurdish villages. Uh.. connected
to Afrin... I mean fifty, sixty years ago they were all
connected to Afrin..

117
00:09:50,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Piştî wê girê dane Niblê.. Wextê me.. Meryemîn e bûn, em bi
ser Efrînê va bûn me qeydên jinkên xwe li.. Efrîn daxistin
e, em e li Efrîn.. qeyd dikirin yanî.. e.
 
After that they connected to Nubl.. During our time.. it was
Meryemîn, we were under Afrin we registered our wives at..
we did it in Afrin, we at Afrin.. we registered I mean..
yes.

118
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:11,000
di wêr ra berê di wêr re em di gundê dadgerî ne, li ser
Basûtê we çûn, û me yanî Efrîn welatê me bû, cihê me bû.
 
We passed through there before, we are in the village of the
court, above Basute you went, and for us, I mean Afrin was
our country, our place.

119
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Hûn ha piştî ev du sed dem ha, hûn ha diketin şoreşê jî, we
jî dev ji gundên Efrînê berneda?
 
You, after these two hundred times, you also joined the
revolution, you didn't give up on the villages of Afrin?

120
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Ê malûm e, me qet dev ji navê gundê me, ser milletê xwe, ser
Kurmanciya xwe...
 
It's known, we never gave up the name of our village, for
our nation, for our Kurmanji...

121
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Ê çawa razî bûn, we digot ev gundê me Şêrawa pirraniya wî,
razî nebû yanî razî nebû, hûn herin ser Neble û Ezazê?
 
How did they agree, you said this village of ours in
Sherawa, its majority, didn't agree, I mean didn't agree
that you go to Nubl and Azaz?

122
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Ê razî nebûn, ê tişt ji dest nedihat der. Yanî tişt ji destê
gundiyan nedihat der.
 
They didn't agree, but nothing could be done. I mean the
villagers couldn't do anything about it.

123
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:52,000
Ê gotin bera neçin gundan me jî em ê çi bikin. Em rabûn me
serî lêxist, nifûsa me li wir bû, mehkeme li Ezazê bû, yanî
hebs cihê mala Ezazê bû. Ne li wir bû.
 
They said they shouldn't go to the villages, and what could
we do. We went and applied, our registry was there, the
court was in Azaz, I mean the prison was the place of Azaz.
It wasn't there.

124
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Ê de spas dikim mala te ava be.
 
Well, thank you, may your house be built.

125
00:10:54,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Ya te jî ava be.
 
Yours too.

126
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:44,000
Di gundê mezin de jiyana xwezayî ya hezar salan heta roja
îro tê jiyankirin.
 
In the big village, the natural life of a thousand years is
lived up to this day.

127
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Jinên gund derdorê daran berhev dikin û di demsala zivistanê
da dişewitînin.
 
The women of the village gather wood around and burn it in
the winter season.

128
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Di vir da hevaltiya mirovan bi xwezayê re li ber çavan
hatiye raxistin.
 
Here the friendship of people with nature is laid out before
the eyes.

129
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:03,000
Gundî bi xwedîkirina pez, dewar û mirîşkan bingeha xwe ya
jiyanî dihunin.
 
The villagers weave their foundation of life by raising
sheep, cattle, and chickens.

130
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Li aliyê din di navbera wan û daran de, jî hevaltiyek kur û
kûr ko dikare hezaran salan hîn zindî ye.
 
On the other hand, between them and the trees, a deep
friendship that could be thousands of years old is still
alive.

131
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Merdî û dewlemendiya exlaqê xwezayî ya gundiyan, heta roja
îro didome û hezkirina mêvanan di nav gundiyan da di asta
herî jor da ye.
 
The generosity and richness of the villagers' natural
morality continue to this day, and the love for guests among
the villagers is at the highest level.

132
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Rojane gundî bi azana dîkan re çavên xwe vedikin û bi demê
re dikevin nav kar û barê xwe yê rojane.
 
Daily, the villagers open their eyes with the call of the
roosters and in time start their daily chores.

133
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Dixwazin ko di zûtirîn dem de, karê xwe biqedînin û piştre
serdana hev bikin.
 
They wish to finish their work as soon as possible and then
visit each other.

134
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Belê temaşevanan hêja, em di vir re derbas bûn, me dît
şivanekî pez di vir e.
 
Yes, dear viewers, we passed by here, we saw a sheep
shepherd here.

135
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Ev gundana jî, bi giştî debara xwe bi pez dikin.
 
And these villages generally make their living from sheep.

136
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Jiber ko vir hemî zinar ne, çiya ne, yanî ne wek deştên din
ne. Wek deşta Hemqê, deşta Cûmê, wek herêmên din ne. Vira
pirraniyê xwe zeytûn tune ne.
 
Because here is all rocky, mountains, I mean it's not like
other plains. Like the Amik plain, the Jume plain, like
other regions. The majority of this place has no olives.

137
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Vira jî pirraniya xwe, debara xwe bi dewar dikin. Niha em
derbas bûn me dît şivanek li vir e, em ê jê bipirsin, navê
wî çi bû?
 
Here too the majority make their living with livestock. Now
we passed by and saw a shepherd here, we will ask him, what
was his name?

138
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Dîbo ye, ehlen wa sehlen.
 
It is Dibo, welcome.

139
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Pêşka...
 
Say...

140
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Navê min Dîbo ye.
 
My name is Dibo.

141
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Ser çavan, navê te çi bû?
 
Upon my eyes, what was your name?

142
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Navê zarok jî Dîbo ye. Navê zarok jî Dîbo ye.
 
The child's name is also Dibo. The child's name is also
Dibo.

143
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Navê zarok jî Dîbo ye?
 
The child's name is also Dibo?

144
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Erê, navê zarok jî Dîbo ye.
 
Yes, the child's name is also Dibo.

145
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Ê kî ye ev?
 
And who is he?

146
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,000
Lawê lawê min e.
 
He's my son's son.

147
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Ha, Xwedê ji we re bihêle.
 
Ah, may God spare him for you.

148
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Xwedê te jî bihêle, tu bi xêr hatî.
 
May God spare you too, welcome.

149
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Te berxikik jî xistiye hembêza xwe ha?
 
You've put a little lamb in your lap too, huh?

150
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Ew em wekî wisa xwedî dikin, dibe ku ew ê nexweş e, me
girtiye bi ser keve inşelleh.
 
We keep it like this, maybe it's sick, we caught it so it
recovers God willing.

151
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Inşelleh.
 
God willing.

152
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Û înşelleh wê serokê me jî derkeve. Inşelleh... Serkeftin e.
 
And our leader will come out, God willing. God willing...
It's victory.

153
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Tu çend sal e şivantiyê dikî?
 
How many years have you been doing shepherding?

154
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Welleh, belkî emrê min ser şêstî re ye.
 
By God, maybe my age is over sixty.

155
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Ê yanî ko çavê te vebûye tu şivaniyê dikî?
 
So I mean since your eyes opened you've been doing
shepherding?

156
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Ê min çaxê çavê xwe vekiriye ez li ber pez bûm, ez li ber
dewar bûm.
 
Yes when I opened my eyes I was with the sheep, I was with
the cattle.

157
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Bavê te jî şivan bû? Kalikê te jî şivan bû?
 
Was your father a shepherd too? Was your grandfather a
shepherd too?

158
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Bavê min, kalikê min, di goran de kalikê min da ev şivan in.
 
My father, my grandfather, up to the graves of my
grandfathers they are shepherds.

159
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:23,000
Dewarê me yên ha ye. Ê ewqas te erdê heye bes erd îşê meselê
xwe, baş e.
 
We have these cattle. And you have that much land, but the
land... its issue is fine.

160
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Erdê me, nîvê wî dehl e, nîvê wî hindik e havê xwe.
 
Our land, half of it is bushes, half of it is little for its
sowing.

161
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Der û dor hemû zinar in.
 
Everywhere around is rocky.

162
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Gi zinar in, gi zinar in.
 
All rocks, all rocks.

163
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Bav û kalên we çawa di vir de dijîn?
 
How did your ancestors live here?

164
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
Genim, ceh, nîsk e.
 
Wheat, barley, lentils.

165
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Di wan nav zinaran de dîsa we diçandî?
 
Did you still plant among those rocks?

166
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Erê me dîsa diçandî, ha ha seke ha pêşiya me ve ha wey ha
dîsa me diçandî.
 
Yes, we still planted, look, look at our front, oh, we still
planted.

167
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Ê gund hemî erdê wan hene? Diçînin ev ji bo?
 
And does everyone in the village have land? Do they plant
for this?

168
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Hene, ê gund hemî ava bû.
 
They do, the village was all built.

169
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Çawan wan zinarana diçandin û hûn çawa diçînin ev di nav de?
 
How did they plant those rocks and how do you plant among
this?

170
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:55,000
Ê dewar alet hebû bi dewarê dajohtin û bi dar dikirin û
dajohtin, ha bi vî haweyî hebû.
 
Well, there were livestock tools with livestock they
ploughed and they did it with wood and ploughed, yes it was
like this.

171
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Ê niha em dinêrin ser şivantî, niha gundê we hemî şivan in?
 
And now we look at shepherding, are all your villagers
shepherds now?

172
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Ê pirr, dewarê wan hene. Ê pirr. Î pirr gî dewar e. Ê ev
dewar hindik e.
 
Well mostly, they have their cattle. Well mostly. Mostly
they are all cattle. And these cattle are few.

173
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Yanî maliyê î gundê dewarê xwe tune ne, hindik in dewarê wan
tine ne wekî di gund gî dewarê xwe ji hebû.
 
I mean, the households of the village don't have cattle,
they are few, they don't have cattle like in the village
where everyone had cattle.

174
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Erê jiber ku Şêrawa bi nav û deng e ji aliyê... mast ve, ji
aliyê penêr ve, ...
 
Yes, because Sherawa is famous for... yogurt, for cheese,
...

175
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Alî şîr, mast de, û alî yanî dewar de, yanî gundê mezin
dewarê xwe ji gundan gî pirrtir bû.
 
For milk, yogurt, and for, I mean livestock, our big village
had more cattle than all the other villages.

176
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Berê de ha. Û nûka dîsa pirrtir in.
 
In the past, yes. And now again they are more.

177
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Yanî her malek çiqas dewara xwe heye?
 
I mean, how many cattle does each household have?

178
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:38,000
We heye, du sed, sê sed wê cem. We heye dused û pêncî, we
heye ev yê min, sed û çil û tiştek pezê min. Sed û dudu pezê
min.
 
Some have two hundred, three hundred together. Some have two
hundred and fifty, some have like this is mine, one hundred
and forty something of my sheep. One hundred and two of my
sheep.

179
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Sed û dudu pezê te ne?
 
One hundred and two are your sheep?

180
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Ew in, ew in.
 
They are, they are.

181
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Ê çêlek jî hene ne? Çêl?
 
And there are cows there too, right? Cows?

182
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
Na, çêl cem min nîn in, me berê çêl hebûn, me firotin.
 
No, I don't have cows with me, we used to have cows, we sold
them.

183
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Li gundî çawa gund? Hene?
 
How about in the village? Are there?

184
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Ê mek biha bû, mek biha bû, ka elek biha bû, û şoxul tune,
me firotin, me firotin.
 
Fodder became expensive, fodder became expensive, see, feed
became expensive, and there was no work, we sold them, we
sold them.

185
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Te tenê firot yan gundiyan gî firotin?
 
Did only you sell or did all the villagers sell?

186
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Na, gî, hineka wekî cem hene.
 
No, all, some still have them together.

187
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Bihêle, vaye hevalê Hesen çêlên wî hene, ê çendek wî hene
çêlên xwe hene.
 
Let it be, look at my friend Hesen, he has his cows, some
still have their cows.

188
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Bes wekî din firotin.
 
But otherwise they sold them.

189
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Niha te berxik jî kiriye hembêza xwe...
 
Now you've put a lamb in your lap too...

190
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Berxka min e, ez jê hez dikim bi canê xwe.
 
It's my lamb, I love it with my life.

191
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Te nav lê kiriye?
 
Did you name it?

192
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Na min hîn nav lê nekiriye. Êni çûçik e.
 
No I haven't named it yet. It's still small.

193
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Ev çend mehî ye?
 
How many months old is it?

194
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Emrê wê... hajdê roj in.
 
Its age... is eighteen days.

195
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Haa nûbî ye?
 
Ah, it's a newborn?

196
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Ê dîbî ye. Çûçik e... Çûçik e...
 
Yes it's a newborn. It's small... It's small...

197
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Ê ka ji me ra tiştekî ser şivantiyê bêje...
 
So tell us something about shepherding...

198
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Jiyana şivantiyê me pez xwedî kir, meselen em berdan pez, me
mêrg û çêre çêkirin...
 
The life of shepherding, we raised sheep, for example we let
the sheep out, we made pastures and grazing...

199
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Û me çêrandin meselen, digerandin, çêra, bilê ku derê çêre
hebû,
 
And we grazed them for example, walked them, grazing, let's
say wherever there was grazing,

200
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Yanî xêr hebû, me dibir wir. Me digerandin.
 
I mean there was bounty, we took them there. We walked them.

201
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Ê ev çend sal in, em nikarin bigerînin... em... me çatir
kirin yanî. Û mentîqeya me Efrîn jî, mentîqe gî dar e.
 
And these past few years, we couldn't walk them... we... we
made it harder for them I mean. And our region of Afrin too,
the whole region is trees.

202
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Cîh pez ko me hebe tune ne, pirr. Cîh boş tune ye.
 
There's no place for us to have sheep, a lot. There's no
empty place.

203
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Hûn pezê xwe nebirin ku derê?
 
Where didn't you take your sheep?

204
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Em ji vir dernakevin naçin der, xaseten ez bi xwe... ez bi
eslê xwe çil sal e ez ji vî gundî ranabim.
 
We don't go out of here, especially me myself... I basically
haven't left this village for forty years.

205
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Tu qet nebû ku derê?
 
You've never been anywhere?

206
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Ez tim mal im, bes ji vî gundî ez naçim derî din naçim.
 
I am always home, I just don't go to any other place from
this village.

207
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Û gundiyên din ew diçin ku deran?
 
And the other villagers, where do they go?

208
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Gundiyên din gî, em diçûn berê, em diçûne, ber bi Efrînê ve
diçûne, Kersanê, em diçûne, Cûmê, Bircikê, Xazewî, Basûtê.
 
The other villagers all, we used to go in the past, we used
to go, towards Afrin we used to go, Kersane, we used to go,
to Jume, Bircike, Xazewi, Basute.

209
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Berya pezê xwe radibûn we diçû...?
 
You used to go after your sheep...?

210
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Me deman dikirin diçûne, me zeman dikir diçûn, me pezê xwe
dibirin, wir diçêrandin.
 
We spent time and went, we spent time and went, we took our
sheep and grazed them there.

211
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Ê vî gavê, meseleya pez wekî pirr çê dibin, wê pez gî pez,
pezeke rind e, û em karê pê nizanin. Seneeta me nîne.
 
And at this moment, the issue of sheep like there are a lot,
it's all sheep, it's good sheep, and we don't know any other
craft with it. We have no craft.

212
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Xwendina me tune.
 
We have no education.

213
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Û xêncî vî karî em nizanin, yanî.
 
And other than this work we don't know, I mean.

214
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Heta karê keviran a em nizanin, yanî ez. Em ne kirin em
nizanin. Nikarin bikin em nakin.
 
Even stone work we don't know, I mean me. We haven't done it
so we don't know. We can't do it so we don't.

215
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Erê bes gundiyên we yên pirraniya xwe karê keviran jî dikin.
 
Yes, but the majority of your villagers also do stone work.

216
00:17:53,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Pirr, pirranî dikin. Elemîne yanî dikin. Hinek di bêşê de
dikin.
 
Many, a majority do. They are used to it, I mean they do.
Some do it in groups.

217
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Ê ka ji me re ser jiyana şivaniyê bêje ji me re...
 
So tell us about the life of a shepherd...

218
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Jiyana şivaniyê... çi bi ser te de derbas bû?
 
The life of shepherding... what has passed over you?

219
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Xweşî.
 
Happiness.

220
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Çi tiştên xweş ji we hatin, ka de di nav de ye zivistan e,
sar e,
 
What pleasant things happened to you, look, you are in the
middle of it, it's winter, it's cold,

221
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Jiyana şivaniyê zemanê xwe de berê çaxê ez cahil bûm,
 
The life of shepherding in its time before, when I was
young,

222
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Heta ku me nîvî çêl û bas dibe, me li derve, pez mexel
dikir. Şivan diçûn digerandin.
 
Even when we had half cows and it was good, we folded the
sheep outside. Shepherds went and walked them.

223
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:25,000
Şev diçûn şevîn dikir, me digerand, şivan... ev çend sal in,
hene dinê, edî erd nema.
 
At night they went for night-grazing, we walked them,
shepherd... these few years, things changed, land was no
longer left.

224
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Hinek bû, hindik bû. Çê di ser zinaran, ser elefan. Yanî
pirr dinê bi dar... dar çandin e.
 
Some was, it was little. Grazing on the rocks, on grass. I
mean the world is mostly planted with trees... they planted
trees.

225
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Dar? Dar çandin ne?
 
Trees? Did they plant trees?

226
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Dar... na mij ve dar çandin e. Yanî wekî sê sal î vir de
xelkê giş dar çandin e.
 
Trees... no since before they planted trees. I mean like
three years ago people all planted trees.

227
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:41,000
Beriya wê dar tune bû. Gi dagirtî bûn, yanî genim, ceh, nîsk
e. Ev tiştana.
 
Before that there were no trees. It was all full, I mean
wheat, barley, lentils. These things.

228
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Ev çend sal in, dema ko dar çandin, dar pê bi xweyî dikin, û
ev çandin e pê çandin e yanî, û giş ev e. Yanî belkî dighêje
çardeh-pênc hezar dar hene.
 
These few years, when they planted trees, they take care of
the trees with it, and this planting is done with it, and
it's all here. I mean maybe it reaches fourteen-five
thousand trees there.

229
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Niha dema tu diçûyî wê şivaniyê te dikir we pez derdixist
tu, kêfa te ji kîjan gundî ra dihat tu diçûyê wira?
 
Now when you went doing that shepherding, you took the sheep
out, which village did you like to go to?

230
00:18:54,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Erê ez biçûma cîranê xwe... gundê xwe... xalên min...
 
Yes if I went to my neighbor... my village... my uncles...

231
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Ez xalê min.. e... xalên min, li wir diçûm cem wan.
 
I went to my uncle... uh... my uncles, I went to them there.

232
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Kî ne xalên te?
 
My uncles.

233
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:05,000
Kî ne xalên te?
 
Who are your uncles?

234
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Ê şivanê ... Ehmed bû navê wî, Ehmed bû, ... ev jî cîranê me
ye.
 
The shepherd... Ahmed was his name, it was Ahmed... this one
is also our neighbor.

235
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Me tim tev hev dikir. Me tev hev dikir... Û yekî din navê wî
Elî ye. Niha... niha jî... li wira şehîd ket.
 
We always went together. We went together... And another one
whose name is Ali. Now... now too... he fell as a martyr
there.

236
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Nav Elî ye, min bi wî ra tev hev dikir. Me tev hev
diçêrandin.
 
His name is Ali, I went together with him. We grazed them
together.

237
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
We pezê xwe tev hev dikir diçêrandin?
 
You put your sheep together and grazed them?

238
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:28,000
Belê, e, yanî me, me ser hezar pezî dikir yek gav em
nizanin... em nas dikin. Nizanin? Me nas dikirin.
 
Yes, uh, I mean we, we made it over a thousand sheep at one
time we didn't know... we recognized them. Didn't know? We
recognized them.

239
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Yanî, medresa me, ev pez e. Wekî din me, me tiştek din
nizanin.
 
I mean, our school, is these sheep. Other than that we, we
didn't know anything else.

240
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
Medresa... me nexwendî. Em nizanin. Tiştê din. Xêncî vî
pezî.
 
School... we didn't study. We don't know. Anything else.
Other than these sheep.

241
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Em pez nas dikirin.
 
We recognized sheep.

242
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Dema hûn pez bi hev ra digerandin, malê xelkê we nas dikir
we diqetand, pezê xwe?
 
When you walked the sheep together, did you recognize
people's livestock and separate it, your sheep?

243
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Na, tenê.
 
No, alone.

244
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Beriya xwe dizanî?
 
Did it know its own first?

245
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Rengê xwe dizane... rengê xwe dizane wê dengê nas dike. Bes
da tu berê mala xwe bifitilî ye.
 
It knows its own color... it knows its own color and
recognizes the voice. Just when you turn towards your house.

246
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Dizane ka tu diçî. Tenê tê cem te.
 
It knows where you are going. It alone comes to you.

247
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Carekê tiştek wisa şaş dikir?
 
Did it ever confuse something like that?

248
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Eh welle, tiştek wisa şaş nekir, te qet nedît te...
 
Eh by God, it didn't confuse something like that, you never
saw it come...

249
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Te digotin, şivantî, yê bilûrê dixe, yê zurnê dixe, yê
stranê dibêjin.
 
You were saying, shepherding, the one who plays the flute,
the one who plays the zurna, the ones who sing songs.

250
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
Pirr... pirr... we, me bilûrê xist, bes em hîn nebûn. Ne
elimîn.
 
Many... many... them, we played the flute, but didn't learn.
Didn't learn.

251
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Te bilûr ji dest xwe girtiye?
 
Have you taken a flute in your hands?

252
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Erê min ji dest girtiye bes hîn nebûm...
 
Yes I have taken it in my hands but I didn't learn...

253
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Ne feş e, ji min re dibêjin te feş paqil avêtiye.
 
It's not a lie, they tell me you threw beans.

254
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Tu bi pîkê dikişînî?
 
Do you smoke with a pipe?

255
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Erê eliyê texm.
 
Yes, roughly.

256
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
Di rojê de çend aliyan tu dikişînî pê, tê de heye?
 
How many times a day do you smoke with it, is there any in
it?

257
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Bes ji mêj da, ji mêj da temenê me de ye û diran jî neman.
 
It has been a long time, it's been a long time, we are at an
age and we have no teeth left.

258
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:15,000
Diranê me ne yê berê ne, yê sînaî ne.
 
Our teeth are not the old ones, they are artificial.

259
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Ma tu dikarî piçekê bikişînî, pîka te tê de heye?
 
Can you smoke a little, is there anything in your pipe?

260
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:19,000
Em dikarin piçekê ji te re... ha tu difikirî? Te amade
kiriye?
 
We can smoke a little for you... oh, are you thinking about
it? Have you prepared it?

261
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Erê min amade kiriye. Wekî cixarê ye yanî em pê diselin.
 
Yes, I have prepared it. It's like a cigarette, I mean we
amuse ourselves with it.

262
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Wî sebra xwe bi pîkê tîne.
 
He keeps himself busy with the pipe.

263
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,000
Erê em pê diselin yanî, em pê diselin.
 
Yes, we amuse ourselves with it, we amuse ourselves with it.

264
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Berê zemanê xwe de dawet pê pîkê, zermeyan diqîrandin.
 
In the old days, at weddings, the pipe would make the sound
of the zurna.

265
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Durbek û def tunebûn. Pîkê zemrê diqîrandin.
 
There were no drums or tambourines. The pipe would sound
like the zurna.

266
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:56,000
[Music]
 
[Music]

267
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Erê bico stira.
 
Yes, sing a little.

268
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Delal bû evana.
 
These were beautiful.

269
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,000
Stranek jî erê wa.
 
Yes, a song too.

270
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:51,000
Delal bû evana.
 
These were beautiful.

271
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,000
Ê kê te eleqadar kir, te ji kê hîn bûye evê?
 
Who interested you, who did you learn this from?

272
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:59,000
Ev maqam e ji berê de, ji gundên Sazbendan rehmetiyê Cemîlê
Horo...
 
This is an old melody, from the villages of the musicians,
the late Cemil Horo...

273
00:21:59,000 --> 00:21:59,000
Na ne Cemîl Horo. Omerê Cemlo.
 
Cemil Horo?

274
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Na ne Cemîl Horo. Omerê Cemlo.
 
No, not Cemil Horo. Omer Cemlo.

275
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Ê ji qewmê Omerê Cemlo, ji qewmê Baqî berê. Em ji wan...
 
Omer Cemlo?

276
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Ê ji qewmê Omerê Cemlo, ji qewmê Baqî berê. Em ji wan...
 
Yes, from the family of Omer Cemlo, from the family of Baqi
in the past. We learned from them...

277
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Berê ev sazben pir bûn.
 
In the past, there were many of these musicians.

278
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:16,000
Vê gavê ew sazben neman, vêgav micesel û tiştî derketin.
 
Right now those musicians are gone, nowadays recorders and
things have come out.

279
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:20,000
Ev sazben neman û ew kes nikarin ne bistirên ne wek berê
neman hewa weha.
 
These musicians are gone and those people can neither sing
nor exist like before.

280
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:24,000
Ê kê piştî te li pîkê dixe? Te ji kê hîn bûye? Ji kîjan alî?
 
Who will play the pipe after you? Who did you learn from?
From which side?

281
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:28,000
Şivan berê diciviyan, şivan û wana heywan diçêrand.
 
The shepherds used to gather in the past, the shepherds and
those who grazed animals.

282
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:32,000
Me jî lêsihet dikir, me jî ji wan hîn bû.
 
We also listened, we also learned from them.

283
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Evana keçika çêkiriye, bi destê xwe çêkirine.
 
A girl made this, she made it with her own hands.

284
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Evana taybetiya... ev a weke yê... destê xwe çêkiriye.
 
This?

285
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:44,000
Evana taybetiya... ev a weke yê... destê xwe çêkiriye.
 
This is special... she made it like... with her own hands.

286
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:46,000
Baş e, em te spas dikin.
 
Alright, we thank you.

287
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,000
Ehlen we sehlen we em jî te spas dikin.
 
You are welcome, and we thank you too.

288
00:22:48,000 --> 00:23:08,000
[Music]
 
[Music]

289
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Kevirên herêmê, bi hezaran salan di avakirina qesr û xaniyan
de hatiye bikaranîn.
 
The region's stones have been used for thousands of years in
the building of palaces and houses.

290
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Niha jî di nav gund de çerxek birîna keviran heye.
 
Now there is also a stone-cutting wheel in the village.

291
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:39,000
Kevirên gund di çerxê ku wekî kargehekê ye têne birîn.
 
The village's stones are cut in the wheel, which is like a
factory.

292
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:42,000
Di vir de bi şiklê tê xwestin têne birîn.
 
Here they are cut into the desired shapes.

293
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Û ji bo tevahiya Sûriyê û gelek welatan derve re têne
firotin.
 
And they are sold to all of Syria and many countries abroad.

294
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:52,000
Kevirên gund di avakirina qesr û xaniyan de têne bikaranîn.
 
The village's stones are used in the building of palaces and
houses.

295
00:23:52,000 --> 00:24:12,000
[Music]
 
[Music]

296
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Belê niha em derbasî vir bûne, ev der jî hemî karê kevira
dikin.
 
Yes, now we have moved here, this place is all about working
with stones.

297
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Gundî hatine vir kar dikin. Kevira çêdikin ji bo malan.
 
The villagers have come here to work. They make stones for
houses.

298
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:43,000
Û ev gundana jî bi taybetî ev karê xwe hene.
 
And these villagers specifically have this work of theirs.

299
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:45,000
Piranî ya pez e, ya kevir ne.
 
Mostly it's either sheep or stones.

300
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Niha em derbas ba wan bibin.
 
Now let's go over to them.

301
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Me go em derbasî cem we bin. Gundê we hemî zinar e, hemî
kevir e, te't in.
 
We said we would come to you. Your village is all rocks, all
stones, all boulders.

302
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:59,000
Belê. Hûn bi keviran re jiyan dikin.
 
Yes. You live alongside stones.

303
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:01,000
Erê wisa ye.
 
Yes, that is so.

304
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:08,000
Zana ev e em, jiyana me... baştir belkî yanî ji bav û kalê
xwe de me dîtiye.
 
You know, our life... is better, maybe we saw this from our
ancestors.

305
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:18,000
Meîşeta me baştir, em bi pez e, ev meqle' baştir millet em
pê jiyan dikin.
 
Our livelihood is better, whether it is sheep, or this
quarry is better, the people make a living from it.

306
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:28,000
Meîşeta xwe, meîşeta em vî gundî piranî karker bi vê
meqle'yê kevira em bi jiyana xwe derbas dikin.
 
Our livelihood, the livelihood of this village is mostly as
workers in this stone quarry, we pass our lives with it.

307
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Yanî em... hefte... şemiyê têne şuxil heta pêncşemiyê çi
kevirê wan rabûye.
 
I mean, we... week... we come to work on Saturday until
Thursday, whatever stones they have extracted.

308
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Çi kevir firotine, pêncşemiyê hesaba xwe, gişt li vir
rûdinin li vir civîn.
 
Whatever stones they have sold, on Thursday they do their
accounting, everyone sits here and gathers.

309
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Hesabê xwe, her yek em bi... çi qas kevir rakiriye, her yek
hesabê wan tê kirin û heqê xwe dibe.
 
Their accounting, everyone... however many stones they have
extracted, everyone's account is calculated and they take
their earnings.

310
00:25:56,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Û pişt re înê naşuxilin. Înê bêhnvedan e.
 
And then they don't work on Friday. Friday is a day of rest.

311
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:04,000
Na ev gundî hemî vî karî dikin? Hemî kevira dikişînin?
 
So do all the villagers do this work? Do they all extract
stones?

312
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:08,000
Bi xwedê piranî, belkî ji sê roba zêdetir e.
 
By God, mostly, maybe more than three-quarters.

313
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:16,000
Ê ku pezê xwe hene, em pezê xwe xwedî dikin, yanî ne hewce
ne.
 
Those who have sheep, they raise their sheep, I mean they
are not in need.

314
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:20,000
Baştir. Ê wan naşuxilin.
 
Better. Those do not work here.

315
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:24,000
Bes ê din sê rib, zêdetirî sê roba giştik jiyana xwe bi
kevir e.
 
But the others, three-quarters, more than three-quarters of
all, their life depends on stones.

316
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:32,000
Yanî cihekî şore wek zinarê me, zinar tunene. Zêdetirî em
jiyana xwe bi kevir e ne.
 
Because there are no rocky places like ours. Mostly our life
depends on stones.

317
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:38,000
Hemî karker dertînin kevir, hemî her hinek li derekê
şuxilin.
 
All the workers extract stones, everyone works somewhere.

318
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:45,000
Em berî vê, berî vê meqle'yê kevira, yanî ne bi vî rengî bû,
çawa bû?
 
Before this, before this stone quarry, I mean it wasn't like
this, how was it?

319
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Em bi kumperês... Kumperês tune bû, meqle' da xurt di kolan
û teqandin. Pê barûtê.
 
With compressors... When there were no compressors, they dug
hard in the quarry and exploded it. With gunpowder.

320
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Diteqandin û em bi ew kevirê mezin derdiketin û bi çakûç
dikirin.
 
They exploded it and those big stones came out, and they
worked with hammers.

321
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Em tevdikaran em qesra bişkênin. Niha ew jî nema. Em bi vê
gavê kumperêsê.
 
We prepared to break the rocks. Now that is also gone. At
this time we use compressors.

322
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Êdî me gavê dawiyê...
 
Now, finally...

323
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:12,000
Meqle' em wek kevirê mezin dertînin, dibin menşera.
 
From the quarry, we extract the big stones and take them to
the saw.

324
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Wana bi semêt diteqînin, û an jî dertînin yên mezin dibin
şûna menşera.
 
They explode it with cement, and they extract the big ones
and take them to the saw.

325
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:22,000
Ema vî demê de hema êdî evê qerneyê yanî ji menşera navê...
 
But at this time, this piece, I mean it's not suitable for
the saw...

326
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:26,000
Gişt traksê wilo çêdike û alî ya.
 
The tractor makes it all like that and puts it aside.

327
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Yanî ê biçûk? Ê biçûk tînin diçe menşerê?
 
Meaning the small ones? They bring the small ones to the
saw?

328
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Erê. Ê biçûk.. û karkerên me em hatin li vir em dixebitin.
 
Yes. The small ones... and our workers, we came here to
work.

329
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Ew karkerana her yek ji xwe ra beşek e, her yek kevirekê xwe
çêdikin, dertînin.
 
For these workers, each one has their own section, each one
prepares and extracts their own stones.

330
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:48,000
Na we çend karker bi we re dixebitin we li cihekî weha?
 
So how many workers work with you in a place like this?

331
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Deh karker hene, deh karker hene.
 
There are ten workers, ten workers.

332
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:03,000
Û bi cuda... cihê din jî hene. Cihê din pir in, milî den,
cida pir in yanî wilo hene.
 
And separately... there are other places too. Other places
are many, on this side, there are many separate ones like
this.

333
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:07,000
Na çend sal e ev çîyayê we, weha nabe yanî tu salan weha
tiştek namîne?
 
For how many years has this mountain of yours been like
this, will there be nothing left in years?

334
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:12,000
Bi xwedê... meîşeta me em... em hemî jê de'îş in.
 
By God... our livelihood, we... we all live off it.

335
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:18,000
Yanî baştirî em van kevira... şuxil tunene. Yanî şuxil
baştirî van kevira nîne.
 
Meaning better than these stones... there is no other work.
I mean, there is no work better than these stones.

336
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Ma hema cihê menşerê, menşerê li ku derê ye?
 
But where is the place of the saw, where is the saw?

337
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:25,000
Menşerê li vî milî ye. Niha em diherin sekînin.
 
The saw is on this side. Now we will go and see.

338
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:45,000
[Music]
 
[Music]

339
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja niha em derbasî vir jî bûn, ev der jî
menşere ye.
 
Yes, esteemed viewers, now we have moved here, this place is
also the saw.

340
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:44,000
Ew cihê ku meqle'yê kevir dişkandin, ev jî keviran mezin
tînin vira...
 
The place where they broke stones in the quarry, now they
bring the big stones here...

341
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Merheba ji we re.
 
Hello to you.

342
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

343
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:52,000
Ew keviran mezin we ji meqle'yê dianin bin menşereyan.
 
The big stones you bring from the quarry to the saw.

344
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:55,000
Bendên mezin em tînin hindir de em alî datînin.
 
We bring the big blocks inside and place them on the side.

345
00:29:55,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Em derbas ba we bin.
 
Let us come to you.

346
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:04,000
Na ev kevirên hûn çêdikin der û ku derê ava kevir e?
 
So these stones you make, where do these stones go?

347
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:10,000
Welle kevirên em çêdikin, heke gund, kelê, kent, taleb ji me
re tên.
 
Well the stones we make, if villages, castles, cities,
requests come to us.

348
00:30:10,000 --> 00:30:14,000
Em dişixulin, derdikeve derve, hasebê hewa ye yanî.
 
We work, it goes outside, depending on the weather I mean.

349
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Hasebê ku varaqek ji me re tê.
 
Depending on when a paper comes to us.

350
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:21,000
Ji Efrînê, ji van gundê dorê me, em dişînin, derdikeve
derve.
 
From Afrin, from these villages around us, we send it, it
goes outside.

351
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Yanî wekî din hûn kar nakin hey ha xwestekek tinebe hûn kar
nakin yanî?
 
So you don't do other work, unless there is a request you
don't work, right?

352
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:28,000
Na na, eger taleb me hebe em dişixulin, tinebe em naşixulin.
 
No no, if we have a request we work, if not we don't work.

353
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Yanî ku derê na li Efrînê û dervî Efrînê derdikeve?
 
So where to, does it go out inside Afrin and outside Afrin?

354
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Derdikeve derdikeve, hawe dewletî derva, Îmarat. Dirê Îmarat
jî.
 
It goes out, it goes out to foreign countries, the Emirates.
It goes to the Emirates too.

355
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:37,000
Wîna bêtir dirê ku derê?
 
Where does it go most?

356
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Dirê Ostoralya, Îmarat, Qeter.
 
It goes to Australia, the Emirates, Qatar.

357
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:43,000
Wina tu derî ku derê balav diki?
 
Where else do you distribute it?

358
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:45,000
Em derê gellek ciyan.
 
We send them to many places.

359
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Na kevirî we çend mitrokî ye? Dema ji we ra tê.
 
Now, your stone is how many meters? When it comes to you.

360
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Kevirê me ji meqle'a ye, kevirên mezin in, vanî, bend in.
 
Our stone is from the quarry, they are big stones, heavy
like this.

361
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:57,000
Em radikin haw bilinc û îvana.
 
We lift them with a crane and such.

362
00:30:57,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Em datînin vir, em diqutînin.
 
We place them here, we cut them.

363
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,000
Û ew li vir qut dikin?
 
And they cut them here?

364
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:04,000
Ê vir qut dikin, û ji vir radikin vê derê.
 
Yes, they cut them here, and from here they lift them to
this side.

365
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Dirabe'înin.
 
They square them.

366
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:11,000
Dirabe'înin 'ardê xwe 30 be 35 be 40 be mitreyek e, em vê re
cahez dikin, dikin sanduqa.
 
They square it, its width is 30, 35, 40 or a meter, we
prepare it here, put it in boxes.

367
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Û şahn tê, radike û dertikeve derve.
 
And the truck comes, picks it up and it goes outside.

368
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:17,000
Wîna nexşan jî çêdikin pê de?
 
Do you make patterns on it too?

369
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:18,000
Nexşa em çêdikin.
 
We make patterns.

370
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Ka di ku derê ye? Wek nexşe wekî kîjan hawî we çêkir?
 
Where is it? What kind of patterns do you make?

371
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:23,000
Vê derê kevirên hanê yên derve ne.
 
Here, these stones are for outside.

372
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:24,000
Û wî nexşe jî li derve çêdikin.
 
And he makes patterned ones outside.

373
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Ka ev çi ye?
 
What are these?

374
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:29,000
Evana lewhe yê destk e.
 
These are boards, handles.

375
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:37,000
Evana yê pê dixe, evana diçirîne, evana tawlê pê têxe, evana
avê pê têxe, evana jî kepse edetî ye.
 
These he puts on, these he tears, these he puts the table
on, these he puts water on, these are regular presses.

376
00:31:37,000 --> 00:31:39,000
Em vê derê dişixulin ewane.
 
We operate them here.

377
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:44,000
Ev jî mesk e e tawlê dirê û tê, û pêşiya min nî şeqale.
 
This is a mask, the table goes and comes, and the front of
me is a pedal.

378
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Na em dikanin kar bikin, em bibînin û binêrin?
 
Now can we work, so we can see and watch?

379
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Em dikanin, ev derê em haw dikin, evane raf'a ye.
 
We can, here we do it like this, these are lifters.

380
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Va kevirên hanî mezin em pê radikin datînin na vir.
 
We lift these big stones with it and put them here.

381
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:58,000
Em datînin na vir, diqutînin, tê ba hevalê min ê ha, ji vir
radikin datîne vir.
 
We put them here, cut them, it comes to my friend there,
they lift them from here and put them here.

382
00:31:58,000 --> 00:31:59,000
Ku derê?
 
Where to?

383
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:03,000
Datîne ser vê derê, evana navê xwe terbî' e ye.
 
They put them on here, this is called squaring.

384
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:05,000
Terbî'e yanî kevir dirabe'îne.
 
Squaring, meaning it squares the stones.

385
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:09,000
Hev kevirên hanê ku menşerê da birîne, derve li ser van naçê
bin.
 
These stones that were cut in the saw mill outside, they are
not processed on these.

386
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:15,000
Rabû û wane... evana ha ne, ev jî terbî'e bes eskî ye me avê
na şixulandiye.
 
Stand up and those... these are like this, this is also a
squaring machine but it's old and we haven't operated it.

387
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:20,000
Evana ha nekî dera hanekî jî, evana cela ye. Kevir
dicelînin.
 
These ones are partly wood and these ones are a polisher.
They polish the stones.

388
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,000
Dûz dikin.
 
They smooth them.

389
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:23,000
Evana jî qesase ye.
 
These are cutters.

390
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Te mînakan... tu dikarî kar bikî na?
 
You gave examples... can you work then?

391
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:25,000
Em dikanin.
 
We can.

392
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:28,000
Hela ka em binêrin çawa tu kar dikî em mêze kin û temeşe
bin.
 
Well then let's see how you work so we can look and watch.

393
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Yallah de binêrin.
 
Alright then, watch.

394
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:53,000
Na wê kî van bişînin vê kevirna? Evana van keviran çi ne?
 
Now who will send these stones? What are these stones?

395
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:55,000
Evana ev kevirana, kevirekî zer e, evê hanî sipî ye.
 
These ones, these stones, it's a yellow stone, this one is
white.

396
00:33:55,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Va sandûqên ji me re tên. Em dikin sandûqan, û şahne dikin
derve.
 
These boxes come to us. We put them in boxes, and ship them
outside.

397
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:02,000
Dirin Qeter.
 
They go to Qatar.

398
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Na wî kî van bişînin Qeter?
 
Now who will send these to Qatar?

399
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:04,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

400
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Ev çend in? Çend sandûqan?
 
How many are there? How many boxes?

401
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:09,000
Em derbê, bîst û çar sandûqa di şahne dikin.
 
We ship twenty-four boxes at a time.

402
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:10,000
Wîna her ro dişînin?
 
Do you send them every day?

403
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:14,000
Na hasebî hewa ye, behsa heftêkî dimîne, du hefte.
 
No it depends on the weather, sometimes it takes a week, two
weeks.

404
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:17,000
Heke h'imlê xwe kemil e, tê radike.
 
If its load is complete, it comes and picks it up.

405
00:34:17,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Ew bixwe tê li vî cihî bardikin?
 
Do they come and load it themselves from this place?

406
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Na ewana şahne tînin em ji wera bar dikin û derbas... haciz
derbas dikin. Teslîm dibin.
 
No they bring the truck and we load it for them and pass...
they pass the barrier. They are delivered.

407
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:27,000
Spas, saet xweş.
 
Thank you, have a good time.

408
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Spas.
 
Thank you.

409
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Jinên gund bi cil û bergên xwe yên herêmî, kurdewariya resen
parastine.
 
The village women, with their local clothes, have preserved
the authentic Kurdishness.

410
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Dûrî sîstema kapîtalîzmê mane, û heta rojên îro civakekî
xwezayî diparêzin.
 
They have stayed away from the capitalist system, and to
this day they protect a natural society.

411
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:50,000
Derd û êşên xwe bi hev re parve dikin.
 
They share their pains and sorrows with each other.

412
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:57,000
Ji ber serweriya jinan a xwezayî, çanda alîkariyê di nav
gundiyan de bi asta herî jor de ye.
 
Due to the natural sovereignty of women, the culture of
helping each other is at the highest level among the
villagers.

413
00:34:57,000 --> 00:35:01,000
Jinên gund di şexsê xwe de jina xwezayî û destana mirovahiyê
rawe dikin.
 
The village women represent the natural woman and the epic
of humanity in their own persons.

414
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:16,000
Da ku civakek li derdorî xwe afirandî pêk anîye.
 
So that they have formed a created society around
themselves.

415
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Belê, naha jî em derbasî orta gund bûn, em me dît dayîk yek,
çar dayîk li vir in, ew jî pincarê dikin.
 
Yes, now we have moved to the center of the village, we saw
a mother, four mothers are here, they are also gathering
wild greens.

416
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Destê we sax bin.
 
Bless your hands.

417
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:28,000
Destê te sax bin, ehlen û sehlen.
 
Bless your hands, welcome.

418
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,000
Ka em berga we nas bikin, navê we çîye?
 
Let us get to know you, what is your name?

419
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Ez dayîka Xelîl im.
 
I am Khalil's mother.

420
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Em hatin em hîro pincarê xwe bikin.
 
Welcome.

421
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:34,000
Em hatin em hîro pincarê xwe bikin.
 
We came today to gather our wild greens.

422
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:35,000
Ka navî we?
 
And your name?

423
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:37,000
Dayîka Xelîl im.
 
I am Khalil's mother.

424
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:38,000
Ser çava.
 
Welcome.

425
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:39,000
Ka metê, navê te?
 
Auntie, what is your name?

426
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:41,000
Dayîka Ednan.
 
Adnan's mother.

427
00:35:41,000 --> 00:35:43,000
Ser çava. Û te?
 
Welcome. And you?

428
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:44,000
Ez dayîka Huseyn im.
 
I am Hussein's mother.

429
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Ser çava me. Ka li vir çi deware ye?
 
Welcome. So what are you doing here?

430
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Wê tiştekî kevin hûn yê bîra me bînin, tiştên wekî gundî.
 
You will remind us of something old, village things.

431
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Ê ev tişte ewe, ji bav û kalan de ye yanî û milet digere
giya yanî.
 
Well this thing is, it's from our ancestors you know, and
people wander the grass you know.

432
00:35:56,000 --> 00:36:01,000
Va pincarên bihara çêdikin, em derin deştan, dikelînin,
dikin şîv, em dixwin.
 
These spring wild greens they gather, we go to the plains,
boil them, make dinner, we eat.

433
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:08,000
Eva tiştekî tebî'et ê yanî, sal bi sal. Di vê biharê de...
bahar çi çêdibe...
 
This is something natural you know, year by year. In this
spring... what happens in spring...

434
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Di kîjan demê dest bi bihar dibe, ev ji çi re çêdibe?
 
In what time does spring start, what are they good for?

435
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Van jî em dibêjin, ha va pincar e. Va jî em dibêjin geztoka.
 
These too we say, look this is pincar. This too we say
geztok.

436
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:18,000
Ev ji nexweşiya sîng re jî rind e. Em dikin cacik tevî
masta. Em vê...
 
This is also good for chest diseases. We make it into cacik
with yogurt. We this...

437
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:20,000
Ev derî dibe hema tu hûn cacik dikin vê?
 
It grows here and you just make cacik out of this?

438
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:22,000
Hê ew l'vir dibe. Ava li vira dibe ew in.
 
Yes it grows here. This is it growing here, those are them.

439
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:24,000
Tamê wê ji xweş e?
 
Is its taste good too?

440
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:27,000
Lê wekî cacikî xiyar e.
 
Yes it's like cucumber cacik.

441
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:29,000
Ku l'vê derî jî tiştin din da hene.
 
There are other things here too.

442
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:31,000
Evana derzîdank e.
 
These are derzîdank (crane's bill).

443
00:36:31,000 --> 00:36:33,000
Ev hema wek tolik e?
 
This is just like mallow?

444
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:34,000
Ê ev tolik e.
 
Yes this is mallow.

445
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:36,000
Eva tolik e ev jî derzîdank e.
 
This is mallow and this is derzîdank.

446
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:38,000
Û ev jî derzîdank e hone. Derzîdan e.
 
And this is derzîdank look. Derzîdan.

447
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:40,000
Û ev jî kerbeş e.
 
And this is kerbeş (thistle).

448
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:44,000
Heva... em hemî tiştên heyî...
 
This... we all the things there are...

449
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Ev hemî tevlihev dibin ewên hûn da bikin?
 
Are all these mixed together that you will make?

450
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Na em gî tevle hev dikin, em bi şûn û bibin, hûr bikin.
 
No we mix them all together, we wash them and go, chop them.

451
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:54,000
Bixwazî çakî ser hêka, kî em bi wê...
 
If you want nice on eggs, we with it...

452
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Hûn bi zeytê çêdikin?
 
You make it with oil?

453
00:36:56,000 --> 00:37:00,000
Ê em destpêkê dikelînin.
 
Yes we boil them first.

454
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:04,000
Dikinê vî şik wek silqê. Çêdikin ser qayxa.
 
They put them in this shape like chard. They put them on
eggs.

455
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:07,000
Û hûn bi tiştin din dixwin û tiştin din li bîra we nayê?
 
And do you eat it with other things and nothing else comes
to your mind?

456
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Na em mas pê... te çi bixwazî dew be, mast be, tu zanî gunda
em bi... pez heye, ga hene, û şîr mast pir in. Em pê dixwin.
 
No we eat yogurt with it... whatever you want, ayran,
yogurt, you know in villages we have... sheep, cows, and
milk and yogurt are plentiful. We eat it with it.

457
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:20,000
Îna ka ji me re carîk di rengî wa bêje.
 
Then tell us their colors again.

458
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:24,000
Çito? Ev tolik e, eva kerbeş e. Û va tolk e.
 
How? This is mallow, this is kerbeş. And this is mallow.

459
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:30,000
Yanî çend qusnûc hebin em nav daberev dikin nakin wa kî li
vê derê, amade.. derzîdank e. Kerbeş e, tolik e.
 
I mean however many kinds there are we gather them now, they
don't do it like here, ready.. it's derzîdank. It's kerbeş,
it's mallow.

460
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:35,000
Em wane divê sor kin, sor kin, çeqir e. Hev rengan e gî
teva...
 
We must fry these, fry them, it's shiny. It's the same
colors all together...

461
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Evana jî çûçik e.
 
And these are birds.

462
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:41,000
Ê baş û xwa çil vir hêşîn e gava tu cida dibin diçin xwa
dicivînin?
 
Okay and why are they green here when you separate and go
gather them yourself?

463
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:44,000
Bi xwa ev tişte gil vir heye.
 
All these things are naturally right here.

464
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:51,000
Lê li dor vir tebî'et e gil vir. Em di vê çaxî salî biharî,
l'gund gî daw pincar heye.
 
But around here it's all nature here. We, at this time of
the spring year, in the whole village there are these wild
herbs.

465
00:37:51,000 --> 00:37:53,000
Xwarina wa jî xweş e?
 
Its food is also delicious?

466
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:58,000
Xwarinê wê jî xweş e û hemî îsan jî dixe.
 
Its food is delicious and everyone eats it too.

467
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:00,000
Ji bo nexweşiya re jî rind e yanî.
 
It's also good for sicknesses then.

468
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:06,000
Lê ji bo nexweşiya re rind e. Yanî ji bo sîng re, ji ewe re
gî rind e yanî.
 
Yes it's good for sicknesses. I mean for the chest, for
everything it's good.

469
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:10,000
Dibêjin yanî gî j' hev re.. j' ewe xwê rind e.
 
They say I mean all of it for each other.. for that it's
good.

470
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,000
Hûn mîrovê hev in mîrî hevdin in jin?
 
Are you relatives of each other, are you wives of relatives?

471
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:14,000
Em cîranên hev in xwişkê me gî hev in.
 
We are neighbors to each other, our sisters are all
together.

472
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,000
Hûn qîzkî hevin e ango?
 
Are you girls from the same place then?

473
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:18,000
Ev jî jina xalê me... ew xaltîka min e ev.
 
This is also our uncle's wife... she is my aunt this one.

474
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Xaltiya te.. ev gundî ti... we li kê derê mêr kiriye?
 
Your aunt.. this village of yours... where did you get
married?

475
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Dew bavê da te... em gir bûn mêr yê hevi ti te zanî.
 
Since the time of fathers... we were together, married each
other you know.

476
00:38:26,000 --> 00:38:28,000
We her duya l' gund e mêr kiriye?
 
Did you both get married right here in the village?

477
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:29,000
Na em li Halebê bûn bere.
 
No we were in Aleppo before.

478
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:31,000
Lê bes gundê te ew e?
 
But your village is this one?

479
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:35,000
Bê ha ev gundê me ye dayîka yê bav û kalan e ew.
 
Yes look this is our village mother, it's the village of our
ancestors.

480
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:38,000
Na rojanî gund ew e ku jin dibêje... gundê bavê te ye yan
gundê kê ye?
 
Now the village days is it the woman saying... is it your
father's village or whose village?

481
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:45,000
Ev e we yê bav û kalan e ew.
 
It is our ancestors' village.

482
00:38:45,000 --> 00:38:48,000
Na niha hûn e rabin van xwarina çêbikin.
 
Now you will get up and cook this food.

483
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:54,000
Ê lê em e na kî wan çêbikin zarokên wa ne dor du dor me pir
bûn malan. Yanî em gî dixwin, em gî bi hev ra ne.
 
Yes we will make them, their children were around us, they
were a lot in the houses. I mean we all eat, we are all
together.

484
00:38:54,000 --> 00:38:56,000
Bi rastî di vê demê de ji dema ku min di dît gundî gîya...
bendarê buharî na, jinan pincar dikişin.
 
Actually in this time, from what I saw, the whole village...
gathering spring crops, the women gather wild greens.

485
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:58,000
Pincar... yanî pincar hemî îsan dixwe.
 
Herbs... I mean herbs everyone eats them.

486
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:59,000
Baş e destê we sax bin.
 
Alright, bless your hands.

487
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:17,000
Spas.
 
Thank you.

488
00:39:17,000 --> 00:39:22,000
Zinar û latên gund her dem sînga xwe ji mirovahiyê re
vekirine.
 
The rocks and cliffs of the village have always opened their
chests to humanity.

489
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:25,000
Û bûne şahidê gelek şaristaniyan.
 
And have witnessed many civilizations.

490
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:32,000
Ji ber himbêzşînwarin di herêmê de diyar dibe ku însan
beriya hezar salan di herêmê de bi cih bûye.
 
Because of the embrace of antiquities in the region, it is
clear that humans settled in the region thousands of years
ago.

491
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:38,000
Li vê herêmê belavbûn û di navê hemî zinar û kevir û latan
de geriyane.
 
They spread in this region and wandered among all the rocks,
stones, and cliffs.

492
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:43,000
Dostaniya mirov bi xwezayê re xweş û zelal di herêmê de tê
dîtin.
 
The friendship of humans with nature is clearly and
beautifully seen in the region.

493
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:51,000
Hemî şaristanên hatine herêmê, xwe sipartine kevir û ji
keviran qesr û xanî ava kirine.
 
All civilizations that came to the region relied on stones
and built palaces and houses from stones.

494
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:57,000
Gelek dîwarên bi hostetiyek mezin, hatine rêsan heta rojên
îro li ber xwe dane.
 
Many walls built with great craftsmanship have been woven
and have survived to this day.

495
00:39:57,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Û dîroka kevnar vedibêjin.
 
And they narrate ancient history.

496
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:08,000
Gundê di bejahiya kû de herêmê de, bajarê roje ji aliyê
bavpîrên kurdan ve hatine avakirin.
 
The villages in the rural area of this region, the city of
Roje was built by Kurdish ancestors.

497
00:40:08,000 --> 00:40:13,000
Lê tişta sosret ew e, bi salan e ev şûnwar hatine
paşguhkirin...
 
But the surprising thing is, for years these historical
sites have been neglected...

498
00:40:13,000 --> 00:40:17,000
Û dîroka wê hatiye bervajîkirin.
 
And its history has been distorted.

499
00:40:17,000 --> 00:40:36,000
[Mûzîk]
 
[Music]

500
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:41,000
Belê temaşevanên me yên hêja, di Gundê Mezin da jî em
derbasî cihên dîrokî bûn.
 
Yes, our dear viewers, in Gundê Mezin we also visited
historical places.

501
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:46,000
Ev tiştên dîrokî kelhek gund e, me got em ê derbas bibin, ez
û mamoste Welat va...
 
These historical things are a castle of the village, we said
let's drop by, me and teacher Welat here...

502
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:50,000
Em dîroka wî em baş nizanin... ew jî belkî baş nizanibe...
 
We don't know its history well... maybe he doesn't know it
well either...

503
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:53,000
Lê me got em ê tiştinî bêjin yanî. Merheba ji te ra.
 
But we said we'll say a few things. Hello to you.

504
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,000
Merheba ser çava.
 
Hello, welcome.

505
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:58,000
Me xwest, em tiştinî dîrokî li vir hene...
 
We wanted to, there are some historical things here...

506
00:40:58,000 --> 00:41:00,000
Belkî bi salan e, bi sed salan e ev e.
 
Maybe it has been years, hundreds of years for this.

507
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:02,000
Tu tiştekî li ser zanî?
 
Do you know anything about it?

508
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Bi xwedê bi rastî cihkî dîrokî ye...
 
By God, honestly, it is a historical place...

509
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:09,000
Û girêdayî dîroka Kurdî ye.
 
And it is connected to Kurdish history.

510
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:12,000
Ew tê naskirin bi navê Bajarê Roje...
 
It is known by the name Bajarê Roje (City of Sun)...

511
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:15,000
Û ew girêdayî dîroka Nabo ye...
 
And it is connected to the history of Nabo...

512
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:23,000
Nabo, yanî pê ve tê girêdan du gundan, xerabeya Kelotê, û
xerabeya Gundê Mezin.
 
Nabo, meaning it connects to two villages, the ruins of
Kelotê, and the ruins of Gundê Mezin.

513
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Bi navê Bajarê Roje, ereban jî vê tarîxa heta dawî nav lê
kirine Xarab Şems.
 
With the name Bajarê Roje, the Arabs have also named this
site Kharab Shams.

514
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:35,000
Ev dîroka xwe vedigere bêtir yanî bêtirî...
 
Its history goes back more, meaning more than...

515
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:40,000
Deh hezar sal, dused hezar sal, du hezar sal berî mîladê.
 
Ten thousand years, two hundred thousand years, two thousand
years BC.

516
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:46,000
Yanî ji dîroka Maron û Sem'anê amûdî wan giya ketine derê,
yanî ev tiştî ye.
 
Meaning from the history of Maron and Simeon the Stylite,
they all belong here, I mean this is the thing.

517
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:50,000
Me xwest em tiştinî zanibin... maxabin em jî nizanin...
 
We wanted to know some things... unfortunately we don't know
either...

518
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:54,000
Bi xwe dîroka me yanî tu dizanî...
 
Well, our history, I mean you know...

519
00:41:54,000 --> 00:42:02,000
Jev cuda... dijmin tim xwestiye jev dûr xistiye...
weşartiye, meselen tineyî kiriye.
 
Separated... the enemy always wanted to keep it far apart...
hid it, for example, destroyed it.

520
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:09,000
Yanî gorî ku em zanin, hasebî meraci'a û ev tiştan, tiştine
taybet in yanî, em bi vî tiştî zanin.
 
Meaning according to what we know, from references and these
things, they are special things, we know about this.

521
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:14,000
Em te spas dikin. Înşellah di bernameyên din da em ê şirove
bikin... vî wextî me jî teng e.
 
We thank you. Hopefully in other programs we will explain
it... our time is tight right now.

522
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:14,000
Spas ji we re...
 
You're welcome.

523
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:15,000
Spas ji we re...
 
Thanks to you...

524
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:17,000
Spas ji we re, û serkeftin ji we re jî.
 
Thanks to you, and success to you too.

525
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:31,000
[Mûzîk]
 
[Music]

526
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:33,000
Belê temaşevanên me yên hêja...
 
Yes, our dear viewers...

527
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:38,000
Li vir em ê xatirê xwe ji we bixwazin, em gihiştin dawiya
bernameya Ax û Welat ji Gundê Mezin.
 
Here we will say goodbye to you, we have reached the end of
the Ax û Welat program from Gundê Mezin.

528
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:42,000
Lê gundî xwestin di dawiyê da govend bigerînin, me jî xwest
em bi we ra bigerînin.
 
But the villagers wanted to dance the govend at the end, and
we wanted to show it to you.

529
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:44,000
Navê wê çiye? Çi dibêjin?
 
What is its name? What do they call it?

530
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Dibêjin zemer e... zemer.
 
They say it is a zemer... zemer.

531
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:47,000
Erebî ye ev e?
 
Is this Arabic?

532
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:49,000
Zemer e, em zemerê lê dixim.
 
It is a zemer, we play the zemer.

533
00:42:49,000 --> 00:42:51,000
Tu kîngê lê dixist ji vê da?
 
Since when have you been playing it?

534
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:54,000
Deh saliya xwe da min lê dixist, heta niha.
 
I've been playing it since I was ten years old, until now.

535
00:42:54,000 --> 00:42:56,000
Pêşî te kê lê dixist?
 
Who played it before you?

536
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:58,000
Pêşî min mezinan lê dixist.
 
Before me, the elders played it.

537
00:42:58,000 --> 00:42:59,000
Wek kê?
 
Like who?

538
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:05,000
Yanî apên min, meriyên min giya lê dixistin, yanî ji kal û
bavên me ye...
 
Meaning my uncles, my relatives all played it, meaning it's
from our ancestors...

539
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:08,000
Ê niha tu ê çi ji me ra lêxî? Çi dixwazî lêxî?
 
So now what will you play for us? What do you want to play?

540
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:11,000
Estranek yanî.
 
A song, I mean.

541
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:12,000
Estranek?
 
A song?

542
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:14,000
Sazekî yanî.
 
An instrumental tune, I mean.

543
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:15,000
Çi sazê? Kîjan a?
 
What tune? Which one?

544
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:16,000
Î reqsê.
 
One for dancing.

545
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:17,000
Ê kîjan a?
 
And which one?

546
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Gulîzer... zêriyê, tu çi dixwazî ez lê dixim.
 
Gulîzer... zêriyê, whatever you want I'll play.

547
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:20,000
Gulê Zêr. De ka kerem ke.
 
Gulê Zêr. Go ahead please.

548
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:40,000
[Zemer û def lê dixe]
 
[Playing zemer and drum]

549
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:20,000
[Zemer û def lê dixe]
 
[Playing zemer and drum]

550
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:35,000
[Zemer û def lê dixe]
 
[Playing zemer and drum]

